  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IPAS Core Contribution 2023-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to IPAS: Ipas&#x2019;s three outcome areas related to access to abortion.
 
Improved policies, laws, and financing: results in this area protect abortion as a human right without barriers limiting access. Financing for abortion and contraception supports affordable and equitable access to services. This is measured by the number of policy changes that promote access to abortion.  

Enhanced agency and social norms: results ensure that social norms support people&#x2019;s ability to exercise their SRHR free from abortion stigma and discrimination, measured through individual belief in ability to exercise their rights (self-efficacy scores).

Improved access, availability, quality and acceptability: Results ensure that pathways to abortion are clear and accessible and that access to abortion is readily available and integrated throughout the health care system, with services that are free of stigma. This is measured by the number of abortions and contraceptive services.

IPAS works systematically to include/promote the rights of persons with disabilities.

Main countries are Benin, Burkina Faso, Cameroon, Cote d&#x2019;Ivoire, Democratic Republic of Congo, Ethiopia, Guinea, Kenya, Madagascar, Malawi, Mali, Mozambique, Nigeria, South Africa, Togo, Uganda, Zambia, Bangladesh, India, Indonesia, Myanmar, Nepal, Pakistan, Argentina, Bolivia, Chile, El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras, Mexico and Nicaragua.</narrative>
  </description>
